"""layers.0.mlp.down_proj:3800 — an indentation-whitespace detector.

What it does: this component goes negative on tokens that are pure horizontal whitespace
(spaces, tabs, non-breaking spaces; no newline), i.e. the indentation at the start of a
code or text line. Its size depends on the run:
  - a run of exactly three spaces (or non-breaking spaces): strongly negative, about -2.2;
  - two spaces: slightly negative, about -0.25;
  - any other run of four or more spaces: moderately negative, about -0.7;
  - any run containing a tab: about -0.6;
  - a single space or a single non-breaking space, and every other token
    (words, punctuation, newlines, indented-newline tokens): 0.

Why: in the model it acts as an "this line is indented" marker that the residual stream
carries forward. The token alone explains most of its variance; context adds little.

Main program: `step` looks only at the newest token's text, so it needs no carry.
"""

