    doc = prefix.document_ids[-1]
    token = prefix.token_strings[-1]
    previous = carry[1] if carry is not None and carry[0] == doc else ''
    value = previous_strength(previous) * continuation(token)
    return (doc, token), float(value)

"""Chat-structure markers give a large positive response.

Message openings, message endings, and thought/tool tags are recognized by
syntax. A message end following a tool-closing tag is weaker than an end
following ordinary text. Sentence punctuation and document starts further
adjust these boundary responses. User/assistant labels in message headers
also receive small responses. Short fragments matching ul + a vowel
(optionally plural s), or ul + ar, receive a negative response. A following
alphabetic token after a fragment ending in ul gets a weaker negative
response. Other tokens predict zero; diverse lexical effects are omitted.
